  "limits": [
    "Ideal SCL clock counts exclude START/STOP timing, setup/hold, stretching, CPU, arbitration, other clients, retries and device power-up",
    "Address-order model assumes a known window and pointer continuity across STOP, with no reset or other display writer; physical behavior remains to validate",
    "ADC model sums listed conversion times and uses a steady periodic complete-cycle tag, not actual INA219 register-latch timing or guaranteed deadlines",
    "Raw-word sweeps verify equations, including words outside usable analog range, not current/voltage accuracy",
    "Phase sweep uses complete-cycle tags in an ideal steady periodic model, not the real CNVR latch or physical sampling simultaneity",
    "No low-line timeout, CNVR clear operation, reset recovery or device power sequence executed",
    "Ten full frames per second in the stress rows is synthetic demand under the cap, not a claim that X0 always emits ten frames or must guarantee completion at that rate"
  ]
